WEBVTT

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.240
<i>The dragons that descended upon 
this world in ancient times</i>

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.190
<i>were reduced to five by a 
disaster sent from the sky,</i>

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.370
<i>forcing them to near-extinction.</i>

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.440
<i>The impact of the disaster sent one 
of them flying into the heavens,</i>

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.090
<i>where it still sleeps.</i>

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.120
<i>That object is most likely 
a fragment of that dragon.</i>

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.700
<i>A fragment that will accelerate</i>

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.630
<i>the end of the world.</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.930
Jezby...

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.310
You are the Dragon Bishop.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.100
Dragon Bishop?

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.020
What does that mean?

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.010
Why did you set that wireworm on Iris?

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.960
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.440
Right before Iris was infected,

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.630
you were the one with her.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.710
Let go of me!

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.000
I'll take her.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.010
You put it on her.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.050
Just like you did to Bayne.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.110
Why would I do that?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.090
What proof do you have?

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.010
When we first met...

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.160
That's all right. I do this every day.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.810
You walked unconcerned into a deep forest

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.570
that was filled with 
monsters to gather fruit.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.130
I never could shake my suspicion after that.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.880
What are you saying?

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.020
When we entered Zagroth...

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.100
The entrance is just ahead.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:46.360
You headed to the village alone, 
saying you wanted to take a look.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.900
When you did, you cast a spell to plant 
memories in all the villagers, didn't you?

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.790
Memories? A spell?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.060
Is something going on?

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:05.070
I remember the look on Dan's face 
when he first saw you, too.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:05.730
Huh?

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.970
I missed you! I missed you so much!

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.890
You're...

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.600
Dan's initial reaction showed 
he didn't know who you were.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.740
I... guess that's true? 
Wait, but back then...

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.110
Back then, you gave Dan your 
own memories using magic.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.650
M-Magic?

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.880
Lanan's current state is proof of that.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.280
Since Lanan suffered from
a mental impairment,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.710
he was the only one unaffected by 
the spell you cast in Zagroth.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.980
I'm not sure when you planted memories 
in the old folks from the settlement,

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.470
but I'm sure it wasn't too difficult.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.060
And the murder of Cox...

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.860
You made the old men do it, didn't you?

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.760
Old "men"? Wasn't Jaca the murderer?

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.230
If Jaca had taken Cox away 
in those conditions,

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.900
there's no way the others 
wouldn't have noticed.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:03.480
After capturing Jaca, 
I interrogated the old men.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.080
Jezby asked us to do it.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.070
My parents died and Lanan ended up that way

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.650
all because of the chief.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.590
Just being with him here is painful...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.380
I just want to die!

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.120
It's not as if we didn't have 
our grievances with the chief.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.600
But we'd never kill him.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.380
Maybe you can give people memories,

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.530
but I guess you can't make 
them do exactly as you want.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:33.150
Wh-Why didn't you tell us 
something this important?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.000
I wasn't entirely sure.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.190
And I ended up sacrificing 
Iris because of that.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.990
This is my responsibility.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:42.780
Glen!

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:43.890
Stop!

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.450
Out of the way!

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.110
Show us who you really are!

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.720
You really are brilliant, aren't you?

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.380
Jezby?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.640
I'm just very distrustful.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.300
I haven't lived the most 
pleasant life, after all.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.620
When I only implant memories,

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.820
odd little mistakes always come of it.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.620
My... real parents?

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:37.650
All people who were born and died in 
the village have a place in my mind.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.200
When I add you and your "real parents,"

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.040
the total is three too many.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.380
I don't know what your story is,

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.260
but don't create any trouble for me.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.160
That's all I want to say.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:57.530
The tiniest rip in the seam 
can ruin everything.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.430
What's that?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.060
That's...

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.790
A flying monster...

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.650
I saw a flying monster.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.720
Just like Iris said...

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.960
I've been riding around on it in search 
of a place to perform the ritual.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.440
<i>I sense many human lives.</i>

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:31.180
<i>If I can use the power in that stone 
to absorb them all at once...</i>

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.920
<i>But there are no settlements 
here, much less cities.</i>

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.650
<i>What does this mean?</i>

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.000
I had no idea Iris saw me.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.320
That was one rip in the seam.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.810
Then, I wanted information on the humans

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.990
that I had sensed near the 
waterfall but couldn't find,

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.320
so I made contact with Bayne,

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.800
but all he told me was some legend he'd 
heard about a place called New Eden.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.790
Eventually, Bayne grew suspicious of me,

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.760
so I infected him with a 
monster and threw him out.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.070
H-How dare you—

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:12.770
Then you heroes just happened to show up, 
so I had you do the searching for me.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.170
Why did you use those monsters 
to destroy Zagroth?

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.600
Because I needed at least a few human 
lives to prepare for the ritual.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.220
M-My mom... was with you at that time.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:28.880
Does that mean you—

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.170
I didn't kill her.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:31.830
But...

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.400
Jezby...

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.910
H-Help...

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.110
Jezby!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.880
You left her to die?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.210
Damn you!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.100
Don't!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.310
No!

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:56.230
Cantil!

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:57.130
Get back!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.270
I can't believe you were the Dragon Bishop!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.400
You didn't notice earlier because 
you're a third-rate sorcerer!

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.130
It's too late now!

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.030
What?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.210
I'm impressed by that hero, though.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.260
It looks like he's fulfilled 
his purpose for me.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.960
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 170 l 0 170

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.960
<b>[Creature Magic 02]</b>

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.960
"Can increase or decrease the persuasiveness of their
own words and actions."
By making one's actions less conspicuous, one can
conceal one's presence. High-level creature wizards can 
even plant new memories in a target by speaking words
imbued with magic. This does not work on monsters that
don't understand speech or people who are not mentally
sound.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.390
Whoa...

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.610
There's an underground city here?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.090
Remember what Cox said?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:37.310
Only those who choose to die 
themselves are led to New Eden.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.130
That's what he meant.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.720
There were some people 
who actually threw themselves

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.600
in here after being run out of Zagroth.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:48.560
Remember when we got trapped 
in those ancient ruins?

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.700
The place Kamilto-san said was 
built thousands of years ago?

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:58.330
They may be people who somehow survived 
throughout those thousands of years.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:02.620
Whatever it is, can't we just bring 
the surviving villagers here?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:06.130
Yeah, we could, but something's bothering me.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.740
Now that I think about it, 
that troll found us too easily.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.290
Didn't it follow our location data?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:16.570
When it did, we just happened to come 
across this waterfall and meteorite,

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.090
and then that city.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.280
Doesn't it all seem too convenient?

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:21.970
You are right.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:22.510
Huh?!

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.420
Isn't that...

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.610
I arranged for it to happen 
that way, after all!

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:34.460
Jezby?!

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.240
But I never would have guessed that the 
descendants of an ancient civilization

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.370
were still living here!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.400
She's a Dragon Bishop.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.200
Glen-san?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.160
Cantil-san!

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.330
Jezby is a Dragon Bishop?

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.590
Secreta eiqua vichten...

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.390
Fragmeitam stella imperion!

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:00.440
Monsters, obey my will!

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.270
They really were being 
controlled with magic!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.550
There are too many!

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.460
Run!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:31.410
Huh?

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:36.460
We're not the ones they're after!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.380
The waterfall?!

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.050
They're after the city on the other side!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.100
Bastards!

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.360
Looks like the boss just showed up!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.700
That thing could flatten 
the city in seconds!

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.390
Thanks, Kusue.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:00.900
No problem.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.920
Why?! Why can't I hit it?!

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.590
Is the meteorite making 
them that much stronger?!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.960
Not only that.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.750
With the power of this fragment,

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:21.060
I could resurrect the 
Great Dragon even sooner.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.180
Wh-What's happening?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.310
Cantil-san! Where's the magic circle?!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.380
I can't find it anywhere.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.520
But it has to be...

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.170
So that's it!

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.000
Cantil-san!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:58.580
Are you okay?!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.730
Don't worry about me...

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.770
Get to the magic circle.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:06.000
The magic circle?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.440
The... golems...

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:08.260
Huh?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.840
They aren't getting 
involved in the fight...

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.270
and there are six of them.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.390
You mean...

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.170
No wonder I couldn't find it.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.900
The whole magic circle was moving around.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.970
Forget about those guys! 
We have to take out the golems!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:26.690
G-Golems?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.920
They should have magic 
circles on their backs!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.620
If we destroy them, they can't 
carry out the blood ritual!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.550
So we just have to get rid of them?!

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.200
So you figured it out.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.180
They're all coming in at once!

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.300
<i>What now?</i>

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.370
<i>I guess we have to get rid of the source.</i>

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:58.900
Yuusuke!

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.100
Take care of things here!

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:01.520
Huh?!

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.800
A plant that absorbs mana?

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.410
Hmph. There's no point in...

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:14.940
When did you...

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:17.460
I can use creature magic, too.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.020
Ah, so you concealed your presence.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.510
And? You think you can defeat me?

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.950
Finis clypeus pito...

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.860
Who knows?!

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.050
Vendyne... Wind Shield!

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.050
No way!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.100
Damn it!

